      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Selective oxidation of Cr and Ta forms a CrTaO4-based surface scale.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6513993::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The CrTaO4-based scale is dense.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6513993::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The CrTaO4-based scale is adherent.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slow growth of the CrTaO4-based scale inhibits further oxidation.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6513993::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Low oxygen diffusivity through CrTaO4 inhibits further oxidation.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial refractory HEA is a uniform solid solution containing Cr and Ta.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cr and Ta concentration controls protective oxide-layer formation during long-term isothermal oxidation.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The relevant oxidation regime includes 1000–1100 °C exposures lasting up to 200 hours.",
